#: gui/main.c:2419
msgid ""
"How the list of files shows each one:\r\n"
"    Name: a good copy is on a drive that is plugged in.\r\n"
"    Name   on <drive>, in italics: its copy is on a drive that is not plugged in.\r\n"
"    Name   - not backed up, in italics: it has no copy yet.\r\n"
"    Name   - changed since backup, in another colour: only an older version is backed up.\r\n"
"    Name   - copy damaged, in bold: the copy on the plugged-in drive is missing or damaged; back up again to fix it.\r\n"
"    Name   - deleted, struck through: gone from its folder; BRODALF still keeps track of its copies.\r\n"
"    Folder   (3 of 10 available): how many files in it have a good copy on a plugged-in drive.\r\n"
"    ★ starred: also copied to your extra places. [encrypted]: encrypted on every drive and extra place it is copied to."
